# Harness file (protected). Where the product's code lives, the source of record for every sensor (ADR 0030).
# It is data, never executed, sourced or included: scripts/harness/layout.sh parses it for the scripts, the
# Makefile and CI (`layout.sh --print` emits only the validated keys), apps/api/tools/harness/layout.go for
# .bin/harness (layout-check, integrity-check's excludes, quality-rows' domains directory), and the domainiso analyzer reads only LAYER_GLOB.
# Every reader fails closed on a malformed file; `make layout-check` (in make check) also checks every path.
#
# KEY=value, no spaces, no quotes, no `$`. Paths are relative to the repo root. A list separates its entries
# with a single `:`. Globs are git pathspec globs: `*` also matches `/` (as in protected-paths.txt).
# Files that cannot read this one (linter configs, CODEOWNERS, protected-paths.txt, jscpd.json, codegen
# configs, ...) name the paths themselves: README.md, "(b) Brownfield project" step 5, lists every one to
# edit with this file. A change here is a harness change: it needs the harness-change-approved label once.

# The Go API module (its go.mod); `.` for a module at the repo root. Its tools/harness and tools/analyzers are
# the harness's own Go modules.
API_DIR=apps/api
# The OpenAPI contract.
SPEC=api/openapi.yaml
# Atlas migrations (with atlas.sum) and sqlc queries.
MIGRATIONS_DIR=apps/api/db/migrations
QUERIES_DIR=apps/api/db/queries
# The generated TypeScript client's package (orval runs there).
API_CLIENT_DIR=packages/api-client
# JS workspaces, each `<dir>/*`: eslint, dependency-cruiser and jscpd read <dir>.
WEB_GLOBS=apps/*:packages/*
# Generated code: never hand-edited, exempt from the suppression check, regenerated by make gen.
GENERATED_GLOBS=*.gen.go:apps/api/internal/*/store/*:packages/api-client/src/gen/*:docs/generated/*
# Product code: a feat touching it needs a spec (rules.md#specs-required-for-features).
PRODUCT_GLOBS=apps/*:api/*
# A domain layer's package, relative to API_DIR: the first `*` is the domain, the second the layer
# (rules.md#go-domain-isolation). Must match at least one package (rules.md#harness-layout-valid).
LAYER_GLOB=internal/*/*
# The sensor groups this product has (ADR 0033): go (the Go API, its contract and the harness itself; always),
# db (Postgres: migrations, sqlc, the schema doc, integration tests) and web (pnpm: the JS workspaces and the
# generated client). A group left out drops its sensors from make check and check-all, its tools from
# make tools, its fixtures from make harness-selftest and, for db, Postgres from make setup. HARNESS_STACK=go,db
# in the environment overrides it for one run.
STACK=go:db:web
# Cross-repo contracts (ADR 0037): optional, and empty here (the template neither vendors nor is vendored).
# Each vendored upstream spec as <vendored spec>@<source repo>@<spec path in the source>@<revision>: the source
# is a host path such as github.com/acme/rooms (fetched over https) or an absolute local repo path; the revision
# is the commit the copy was taken at. make upstream-drift (weekly in drift.yml, never in make check) fetches
# each source's head and reports its breaking changes against the vendored copy
# (rules.md#api-upstream-no-breaking-change). Refresh a copy and its revision together.
UPSTREAM_SPECS=
# Repos that vendor this repo's contract, such as github.com/acme/web: contract-check.sh names them when a
# change breaks the contract (rules.md#api-no-breaking-change), so its approval stands for a multi-repo change.
CONTRACT_CONSUMERS=
